# Files over 5 MB written by scripts; their SHA-256 digests are recorded in the writing script's manifest.
# scripts/g19_run_preseal.py (manifests/g19_run_preseal.json > outputs, files_over_5MB)
evaluation/preseal/predictions/V0__rows.parquet

# --- the completed discovery run's raw fold records (240.3 MB) ----------------------------------
# Same convention as generations/gen18_process/.gitignore and generations/gen16_leads/.gitignore:
# the raw search output is excluded by design, its SHA-256 is recorded in
# evaluation/discovery/MANIFEST.sha256, and everything a decision file or the report cites by
# number lives in a small committed CSV, JSON or Markdown file.
#
# Every fitted fold writes one record pair
#   evaluation/discovery/<arm>/<design>/s<seed>/<metal state>[__<cell hash>].{parquet,json}
# -- the per-row predictions and the record's provenance block (fold digest, resume digest,
# below-footer prereg digest, addenda digest, code digest, registry stage).  3,900 files, 224.0 MB:
# 1,461 registered records over the 7 fitted arms (B5, B6, B6r0, B8, FLAT_CAT, M1, M2), the 488
# shared _support frames and the _s1c_yardsticks refit, as .parquet + .json pairs; plus the runner's
# 16.3 MB stdout log.
#
# What stays in version control (NOT matched by the two patterns below): the scorer's outputs
# evaluation/discovery/{contrasts_registered,contrasts_exploratory,r19_items,records_index}.csv,
# the decision files evaluation/discovery/decisions/*.json (decisions, stop_rule, plan_state,
# record_verification, wall_clock, b6_checks), the cost model and job plan under
# evaluation/discovery/benchmark/, the start-of-run leakage safeguard certificates under
# evaluation/discovery/safeguard/, and every table under tables/ (discovery_summary.{csv,md},
# discovery_contrasts.md, discovery_comparator_intervals.csv, discovery_pair_summary.csv,
# discovery_coverage_by_domain_status.csv).
#
# A record is NEVER re-verified against live code or live text (POST-HOC addendum 2 item 5): the
# digests it carries are compared with manifests/digest_registry.json, stage `discovery`
# (code 895a6ab9..., below-footer 05f36fc0..., 1,461 records) or `discovery_candidates`.  So a
# regenerated run is compared with the one the decisions were written from through this manifest,
# not by re-running a verifier against whatever the tree now holds.
#
# Regenerate (76.6 h wall clock on 2 workers / 12 threads, 60 h budget exhausted at 62.1 h):
#   PYTHONIOENCODING=utf-8 PYTHONPATH=generations/gen19_chem_transfer .venv/Scripts/python.exe \
#       generations/gen19_chem_transfer/scripts/g19_run_discovery.py --workers 2
# Verify what is present:
#   .venv/Scripts/python.exe generations/gen19_chem_transfer/scripts/g19_manifest_discovery.py --check
evaluation/discovery/*/*/s*/
evaluation/discovery/logs/

# --- the once-only confirmation run's raw fold records (RUN IN PROGRESS) -----------------------
# Same convention as the discovery block above: the raw per-fold output is excluded by design and
# its SHA-256 is recorded in evaluation/confirmation/MANIFEST.sha256, written by
#   .venv/Scripts/python.exe generations/gen19_chem_transfer/scripts/g19_manifest_discovery.py --root confirmation
# (verify with --check --root confirmation).
#
# Every fitted fold writes one record pair
#   evaluation/confirmation/records/<arm>[/<leg>]/<design>/i<seed index>/<fold>.{parquet,json}
# -- per-row predictions plus the record's provenance block (fold digest, resume digest, below-footer
# prereg digest, addenda digest, code digest, registry stage).  The seed INDEX i1..i5 appears in the
# path, never a seed VALUE: the five withheld seeds enter only through --seed-store and are revealed
# in decisions/CONFIRMATION.md after the run (pre-registration section 15, POST-HOC addendum 6 item 4).
#
# What stays in version control (NOT matched by the pattern below): the withheld-seed fold DESIGNS
# under evaluation/confirmation/folds/ (4.7 MB -- the evidence of which folds each seed index
# produced, and no seed is recoverable from one), the run's stdout logs under
# evaluation/confirmation/logs/ (26 KB), the once-only lock decisions/run_started.json,
# RUN_STATUS.md, and -- once the run finishes -- decisions/confirmation.json, decisions/CONFIRMATION.md
# and every table the report cites.
#
# Resume after ANY interruption (it re-fits no completed fold and re-scores no claim): run
# scripts/g19_run_confirmation.py with --resume and --seed-store, per RUN_STATUS.md.
evaluation/confirmation/records/
